rs during a meeting with technology executives about artificial intelligence in the East Room of the White House on Sept. 29.", "source_id": "SOURCE-F2713022315255015DAEF71D", "temporal_status": null, "text": "President Trump speaks with Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang and others during a meeting with technology executives about artificial intelligence in the East Room of the White House on Sept. 29."}, {"claim_status": null, "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "MEM-EVID-5AB3DE7E822691295FEBB259", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "President Donald Trump on Tuesday announced that the US government would rename artificial intelligence \"super intelligence\" in official communications, as world leaders jostled over how to address the dangers of the fast-advancing technology.", "source_id": "SOURCE-7EA7844C9D194FECD5069C88", "temporal_status": null, "text": "President Donald Trump on Tuesday announced that the US government would rename artificial intelligence \"super intelligence\" in official communications, as world leaders jostled over how to address the dangers of the fast-advancing technology."}, {"claim_status": "reported_claim", "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-1419971820F164C837933207", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "Anthropic , Google and OpenAI aim to launch a standards body focused on artificial intelligence (AI) by the end of this year or early next year, The Information reported Thursday (Sept. 24), citing unnamed sources.", "source_id": "SOURCE-3112A158BFE36AC1CAC41132", "temporal_status": "unknown", "text": "Anthropic , Google and OpenAI aim to launch a standards body focused on artificial intelligence (AI) by the end of this year or early next year, The Information reported Thursday (Sept. 24), citing unnamed sources."}, {"claim_status": "reported_claim", "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-BF69D9417CED98DE228AF5EF", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "They initially aimed to form a public-private partnership, but that effort stalled in the Trump administration, according to the report.", "source_id": "SOURCE-3112A158BFE36AC1CAC41132", "temporal_status": "unknown", "text": "They initially aimed to form a public-private partnership, but that effort stalled in the Trump administration, according to the report."}, {"claim_status": "reported_claim", "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-A5E6571233414CD5E71D2DBF", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "The standards body would support third-party organizations that test models before they are deployed, would detail how AI developers should report safety and security incidents, would define the labs' voluntary safety and security commitments, and would establish qualifications for independent auditors of models and labs, the report said.", "source_id": "SOURCE-3112A158BFE36AC1CAC41132", "temporal_status": "unknown", "text": "The standards body would support third-party organizations that test models before they are deployed, would detail how AI developers should report safety and security incidents, would define the labs' voluntary safety and security commitments, and would establish qualifications for independent auditors of models and labs, the report said."}, {"claim_status": "reported_claim", "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-245A149FE0C97FAB74844B4F", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "The White House Accord on Super Intelligence was signed on September 29 by executives from Google, Anthropic, Meta, OpenAI, xAI, and NVIDIA.", "source_id": "SOURCE-34DAD6C0566224EE443C2C91", "temporal_status": "unknown", "text": "The White House Accord on Super Intelligence was signed on September 29 by executives from Google, Anthropic, Meta, OpenAI, xAI, and NVIDIA."}, {"claim_status": "reported_claim", "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-EBAACD8E95EA95393688FFFD", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "Six major AI companies have agreed to voluntary safety commitments with the White House, establishing internal controls, independent audits, and board-level oversight for advanced AI models.", "source_id": "SOURCE-34DAD6C0566224EE443C2C91", "temporal_status": "unknown", "text": "Six major AI companies have agreed to voluntary safety commitments with the White House, establishing internal controls, independent audits, and board-level oversight for advanced AI models."}, {"claim_status": "reported_claim", "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-01D2908BB02346E3A7C52361", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "Status as of September 30, 2026: the accord text is available as a one-page document posted to the President's Truth Social account and reprinted by news outlets.", "source_id": "SOURCE-5F4AF27BB413D1A1D56AF783", "temporal_status": "unknown", "text": "Status as of September 30, 2026: the accord text is available as a one-page document posted to the President's Truth Social account and reprinted by news outlets."}, {"claim_status": "reported_claim", "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-621554D75011C989E986B63A", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "What is it? A one-page voluntary AI safety standards accord signed September 29, 2026 by the President and leaders of Google, Anthropic, Meta, OpenAI, xAI, and Nvidia.", "source_id": "SOURCE-5F4AF27BB413D1A1D56AF783", "temporal_status": "unknown", "text": "What is it? A one-page voluntary AI safety standards accord signed September 29, 2026 by the President and leaders of Google, Anthropic, Meta, OpenAI, xAI, and Nvidia."}, {"claim_status": "reported_claim", "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-CF2A043EE3E31C6876540651", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "Speaking to reporters, Zuckerberg said the companies agreed to \"multiple layers of auditing and controls,\" including internal evaluations and external audits, as reported by CBS News.", "source_id": "SOURCE-5F4AF27BB413D1A1D56AF783", "temporal_status": "unknown", "text": "Speaking to reporters, Zuckerberg said the companies agreed to \"multiple layers of auditing and controls,\" including internal evaluations and external audits, as reported by CBS News."}, {"claim_status": "reported_claim", "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-4A17E20338015CF71A5E4730", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "Asked whether it was binding, the President said, \"I think it's morally binding,\" according to CBS News.", "source_id": "SOURCE-5F4AF27BB413D1A1D56AF783", "temporal_status": "unknown", "text": "Asked whether it was binding, the President said, \"I think it's morally binding,\" according to CBS News."}, {"claim_status": "reported_claim", "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-59F53A081F442C5F986BEB86", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "AMD has named OneQode as a cloud service provider in the AMD InstinctTM GPU Evaluation Program.", "source_id": "SOURCE-552AE9272E342EEEDF1A5B54", "temporal_status": "unknown", "text": "AMD has named OneQode as a cloud service provider in the AMD InstinctTM GPU Evaluation Program."}, {"claim_status": "reported_claim", "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-A54067BEBF3AC05BCF92D89D", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "Here is a number to sit with: $10 billion . That is what investors now say a personal AI assistant called Instinct is worth, after it raised a $1 billion Series C led by Sequoia Capital, with Benchmark and Coatue along for the ride ( Pulse 2.0 ).", "source_id": "SOURCE-CA5042B5CC34665658BF9040", "temporal_status": "unknown", "text": "Here is a number to sit with: $10 billion . That is what investors now say a personal AI assistant called Instinct is worth, after it raised a $1 billion Series C led by Sequoia Capital, with Benchmark and Coatue along for the ride ( Pulse 2.0 )."}, {"claim_status": "reported_claim", "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-9183955DB4D75E6146CE27D5", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "Roughly one month earlier, Instinct had raised a $250 million Series B at a $2.5 billion valuation , co-led by Index Ventures and Benchmark ( Layer3 Labs ).", "source_id": "SOURCE-CA5042B5CC34665658BF9040", "temporal_status": "unknown", "text": "Roughly one month earlier, Instinct had raised a $250 million Series B at a $2.5 billion valuation , co-led by Index Ventures and Benchmark ( Layer3 Labs )."}, {"claim_status": "reported_claim", "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-3CE5C86ABCE9E31CA3140AB5", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "What makes that leap unusual: Instinct still runs invite-only, has not shipped a mobile app, and has disclosed zero user numbers and zero revenue ( Phemex ).", "source_id": "SOURCE-CA5042B5CC34665658BF9040", "temporal_status": "unknown", "text": "What makes that leap unusual: Instinct still runs invite-only, has not shipped a mobile app, and has disclosed zero user numbers and zero revenue ( Phemex )."}, {"claim_status": "reported_claim", "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-F569722D104741B0E18AA760", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "\"We're building Instinct to be the best personal agent that can handle the deeply personal nuances of everyday life. This funding helps us bring Instinct to more people and continue building the future of personal AI.\" - Noah Shinn, founder of Instinct", "source_id": "SOURCE-CA5042B5CC34665658BF9040", "temporal_status": "unknown", "text": "\"We're building Instinct to be the best personal agent that can handle the deeply personal nuances of everyday life. This funding helps us bring Instinct to more people and continue building the future of personal AI.\" - Noah Shinn, founder of Instinct"}, {"claim_status": "reported_claim", "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-84ED1B9DC5B5B0065923391B", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "Cloud and security giant Akamai on Tuesday announced plans to acquire application programming interface (API) protection company Noname Security.", "source_id": "SOURCE-9C9B8123C6BC102F070C7E61", "temporal_status": "unknown", "text": "Cloud and security giant Akamai on Tuesday announced plans to acquire application programming interface (API) protection company Noname Security."}, {"claim_status": "reported_claim", "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-77D56FF6D9ACFA284B74AD74", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "Research shows that 50.7% of organizations rely on public AI tools such as ChatGPT and Copilot but only 20.2% report enterprise-wide AI deployments built on a governed framework.", "source_id": "SOURCE-31FBFB78F9282C827C68A7D2", "temporal_status": "unknown", "text": "Research shows that 50.7% of organizations rely on public AI tools such as ChatGPT and Copilot but only 20.2% report enterprise-wide AI deployments built on a governed framework."}, {"claim_status": "reported_claim", "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-6202AF36A7385CE7A8B303B5", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "Under a partnership, the Simons Foundation, Anthropic and OpenAI will commit $15 million in combined funding and resources.", "source_id": "SOURCE-F81BAC1883B01771CD02CC09", "temporal_status": "unknown", "text": "Under a partnership, the Simons Foundation, Anthropic and OpenAI will commit $15 million in combined funding and resources."}, {"claim_status": "reported_claim", "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-F85EDA8DD5FBADAAF9AFCF88", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "Anthropic and OpenAI will also provide AI tools and computing resources to a select group of researchers supported by the Simons Foundation, extending beyond mathematics to include basic science.", "source_id": "SOURCE-F81BAC1883B01771CD02CC09", "temporal_status": "unknown", "text": "Anthropic and OpenAI will also provide AI tools and computing resources to a select group of researchers supported by the Simons Foundation, extending beyond mathematics to include basic science."}, {"claim_status": "reported_claim", "event_id": "", "evidence_id": "EVID-2B662527CB207440B1310128", "evidence_type": "source_excerpt", "source_excerpt": "Voluntary Environmental Commitments go beyond mandatory regulations and allow companies to adopt specific commitments to reduce their environmental footprint. In other words, organizations propose appropriate technical solutions and self-imposing commitments that, once acquired, cease to be voluntary, and the company is obliged to comply with them.", "source_id": "SOURCE-A144B5DF8458E92CC9CAC3D8", "temporal_status": "unknown", "text": "Voluntary Environmental Commitments go beyond mandatory regulations and allow companies to adopt specific commitments to reduce their environmental footprint. In other words, organizations propose appropriate technical solutions and self-imposing commitments that, once acquired, cease to be voluntary, and the company is obliged to comply with them."}], "forecast_followups": {"open": [], "resolved": [], "summary": {"check_failures": 0, "checked_with_new_evidence": 0, "contradicted": 0, "deferred_due_check_budget": 0, "expired": 0, "observed": 0, "open_before": 0, "persisted": false, "recorded_this_run": 0, "still_open": 0, "version": "forecast-followup-v2"}, "track_record": {"counts": {}, "decided": 0, "observed_share": null}}, "grounding_by_insight": {"INSIGHTREV-2B67888E65A4F9CCE789BA13": {"claim_count": 1, "claims": [{"attribution_valid": true, "citation_valid": true, "cited_evidence_ids": ["EVID-6FED6EAF5E10A1BE0845C753", "EVID-41CC34E7372A3FAC8D976C8F", "EVID-6710BDB7A5A076547782678B", "EVID-1419971820F164C837933207", "EVID-6202AF36A7385CE7A8B303B5", "EVID-F85EDA8DD5FBADAAF9AFCF88", "EVID-C73C20FD74852CFF04D3CDEE", "EVID-2B662527CB207440B1310128"], "claim_id": "INSIGHTREV-2B67888E65A4F9CCE789BA13-INSIGHT-01", "claim_text": "While President Donald Trump signed a voluntary AI safety accord and OpenAI publicly affirmed it pauses training or holds back models when needed to safely manage capability, OpenAI simultaneously committed $15 million in combined funding and resources with Anthropic and the Simons Foundation. [ASSUMPTION] Because federal safety frameworks rely on voluntary commitments without statutory enforcement thresholds, model providers retain exclusive discretion over operational pause triggers. [ASSUMPTION] Consequently, OpenAI will maintain its joint resource commitments with the Simons Foundation and rely on internal governance rather than external regulatory mandates to govern model release timelines.", "contradicted_evidence_ids": [], "epistemic_type": "hidden_insight", "grounding_status": "inference_supported", "invalid_evidence_ids": [], "metadata": {"candidate_evidence_count": 8, "claim_fingerprint": "1feea564511e99e3ac7c4354174a1e86a7d141f8bba819fbd61429f9703c4275", "evidence_fingerprint": "c6127a502d1c97ad3135da44b992b7616b0f4681a4ab2aefb7aa1dfcb9d786cf", "model": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "prompt_version": "grounding-v1.3-context-first"}, "multi_evidence_required": true, "multi_evidence_satisfied": true, "numeric_valid": true, "rationale": "The evidence directly supports that President Donald Trump signed a voluntary AI accord, OpenAI stated it pauses training when needed for safety, OpenAI and the Simons Foundation (along with Anthropic) committed $15 million in combined funding and resources, and the accord is voluntary. The final conclusion that OpenAI will maintain its commitments and rely on internal governance rather than regulatory mandates is a reasonable explicit inference derived from these premises.", "supporting_evidence_ids": ["EVID-6FED6EAF5E10A1BE0845C753", "EVID-41CC34E7372A3FAC8D976C8F", "EVID-6710BDB7A5A076547782678B", "EVID-6202AF36A7385CE7A8B303B5", "EVID-C73C20FD74852CFF04D3CDEE"], "temporal_valid": true, "unsupported_parts": [], "valid_evidence_ids": ["EVID-6FED6EAF5E10A1BE0845C753", "EVID-41CC34E7372A3FAC8D976C8F", "EVID-6710BDB7A5A076547782678B", "EVID-1419971820F164C837933207", "EVID-6202AF36A7385CE7A8B303B5", "EVID-F85EDA8DD5FBADAAF9AFCF88", "EVID-